{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-wenzl-A-operator","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:wenzl-A-operator","kind":"definition","title":"Wenzl A-operator $A^\\lambda_{\\mu\\nu}(I)$: the $(\\mu, \\nu)$-block of an interface generator","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-lr-coefficient-hecke"],"cites":["references/wenzl1988","references/hoefsmit1974"],"tags":["wenzl-a-operator","operator-valued","hecke-branching","littlewood-richardson","sub-lemma-2-1","section-3b-cond"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator","text":"wenzl-A-operator.md","leanSource":"wenzl-A-operator.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:wenzl-A-operator\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\vdash n</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = n_1 + n_2</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I = \\sigma_{n_1} \\in \\mathbf{H}_n(q)</code> be the inter-block interface generator joining <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{H}_{n_1}(q)</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbf{H}_{n_2}(q)</code>. In the Wenzl 1988 Littlewood–Richardson decomposition of the restriction <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">V_\\lambda \\downarrow_{\\mathbf{H}_{n_1} \\otimes \\mathbf{H}_{n_2}}</code>, the <strong>Wenzl A-operator</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A^\\lambda_{\\mu\\nu}(I)</code> is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mu, \\nu)</code>-block of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> acting on the corresponding isotypic summand:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  A^\\lambda_{\\mu\\nu}(I) \\;\\in\\; \\mathrm{End}(V_\\mu \\otimes V_\\nu)^{\\oplus c^\\lambda_{\\mu\\nu}},</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c^\\lambda_{\\mu\\nu}</code> is the Littlewood–Richardson coefficient.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.7.64","page":"b/def-wenzl-a-operator","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.WenzlAOperator","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-A-operator.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
